1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
READING TASK

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,720
Journey Down the Mekong Part 6

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,940
The End of Our Journey

4
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:14,540
Cambodia was in many ways similar to Laos, although it has twice the population.

5
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:21,140
At another inn we talked with a teacher who told us that half of the people in her country

6
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,320
couldn't read or write.

7
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,940
Her village couldn’t even afford to build a school,

8
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,760
so she had to teach outside under a large tent.

9
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:36,660
When we said goodbye, we all felt very lucky to have studied in college.

10
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:41,820
Back on the road, we passed between many hills and forests.

11
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:46,740
Then we came to the plains and entered Phnom Penh(金边),

12
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,400
the capital of Cambodia.

13
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:54,000
In many ways it looked like Vientiane and Ho Chi Minh City;

14
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:59,560
it also had wide streets with trees in rows and old French houses.

15
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:05,180
Unlike Vientiane, ships could travel the Mekong River here.

16
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:16,480
It can only be seen outside the palace on special days.

17
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:23,440
We ate an early supper and went to see a great temple with floors made of silver.

18
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,340
The next morning our group slept late.

19
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,160
We were very tired from the long bike ride the day before.

20
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,600
Cycling in the hills had been difficult.

21
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:40,540
Now our cousins had the chance to make jokes about Wang Wei

22
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,240
and me.

23
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,060
Perhaps, they said, they were the strong ones!

24
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:49,020
We had lunch at a nice outdoor cafe.

25
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,400
then rode out of the city.

26
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:55,620
Two days later we crossed the border into Vietnam.

27
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,860
We began to see many more people,

28
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,760
but I wasn’t surprised.

29
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:08,880
I read in an atlas before our trip that Vietnam has almost seven times the population of Cambodia.

30
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:17,900
We met a farmer who gave us directions and told us that he grows a new rice crop four times every year

31
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,920
so he can feed more people.

32
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:25,860
He also told us that the northern part of his country has many mountains

33
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:29,000
and it is much cooler than here in the south,

34
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,320
where it is flat.

35
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:34,840
Although the flat delta made it easier for us to cycle,

36
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,340
we got warm very quickly.

37
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:41,980
So we drank lots of water and ate lots of bananas.

38
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,120
Soon the delta separated into nine smaller rivers.

39
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:52,300
Two days later, after we had passed thousands of rice fields,

40
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,160
we came to the sea.

41
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:57,640
We were tired but also in high spirits:

42
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:03,300
our dream to cycle along the Mekong River had finally come true.
